  "interpretation": [
    "With caption content retained from aligned PRISM, native-prefix substitution reduces excess mean matched flow MSE over native by 98.57% on training probes and 98.12% on heldout probes. Adding native suffix produces no consistent further improvement over prefix-only.",
    "Aligned content features are much closer to native after RMSNorm than the unsupervised template regions: training prefix/content/suffix MSE means are approximately 0.6383/0.03055/1.15175; heldout means are 0.63818/0.05722/1.14063. Despite the larger suffix feature MSE, prefix substitution has the dominant measured flow effect.",
    "Wrong-caption preference and absolute denoising error answer different questions. All heldout routes prefer the correct caption on all six target-timestep cases, while aligned PRISM still has much higher matched loss than native. A larger positive caption gap is not automatically better image quality.",
    "The evidence supports testing explicit prefix/content/suffix alignment before attributing the gap to dataset size or frozen VLM inadequacy. This is a next-experiment rationale, not a guarantee that such training will match the teacher.",
    "This run contains only two training and two heldout targets, three timesteps each, and two caption-only generated examples per route. Hybrids use the native teacher and do not establish deployable PRISM-only generation or generalization. No accuracy, FID, reconstruction, or benchmark claim is made."
  ],
  "quality_benchmark": false,
  "training_performed": false
